WEBVTT

1
00:03:36.592 --> 00:03:38.512
Inmate 2537.

2
00:03:41.388 --> 00:03:43.428
Report to the Sergeant's office.

3
00:03:49.605 --> 00:03:51.145
<i>Mom passed away.

4
00:03:55.194 --> 00:03:58.914
<i>John posted bond so you can come here.

5
00:04:00.991 --> 00:04:02.491
<i>You have to come.

6
00:04:09.250 --> 00:04:10.500
Okay.

7
00:04:20.177 --> 00:04:23.557
You do need report back here
in 72 hours.

8
00:04:24.098 --> 00:04:28.768
You will be called often
on this phone to confirm your location.

9
00:04:29.144 --> 00:04:31.614
If ever you do not answer that phone,

10
00:04:31.605 --> 00:04:33.685
you will be declared a fugitive

11
00:04:33.774 --> 00:04:36.444
and a warrant will be issued
for your immediate apprehension.

12
00:04:36.735 --> 00:04:37.985
You understand?

13
00:04:41.282 --> 00:04:42.532
Yes sir.

14
00:05:38.839 --> 00:05:40.669
It's alright, ma'am,
welcome aboard.

15
00:06:45.989 --> 00:06:48.329
Stop! Stop! Stop!

16
00:06:55.833 --> 00:06:57.793
Living dangerously, are we.
Buddy?

17
00:06:58.043 --> 00:06:59.213
Sorry.

18
00:06:59.795 --> 00:07:00.835
Ticket.

19
00:07:01.171 --> 00:07:02.091
Ok.

20
00:07:04.508 --> 00:07:05.678
Oh, shit!

21
00:07:06.093 --> 00:07:08.723
I don't have all day, buddy.
It's 68 bucks.

22
00:07:12.141 --> 00:07:13.431
Ok. Hold on.

23
00:07:19.440 --> 00:07:20.980
Excuse me...

24
00:07:26.447 --> 00:07:30.157
I lost my wallet.
Do you have maybe 30 bucks?

25
00:07:51.930 --> 00:07:53.140
Thank you.

26
00:07:59.146 --> 00:08:02.516
Sorry, my friend lost my ticket.

27
00:08:02.649 --> 00:08:03.979
Here is your ticket.

28
00:08:05.652 --> 00:08:06.822
Thank you.

29
00:08:28.509 --> 00:08:29.929
Are you Chinese?

30
00:08:34.306 --> 00:08:35.346
Yes.

31
00:08:36.058 --> 00:08:37.228
Nice to meet you.

32
00:08:37.684 --> 00:08:39.654
Sorry I'm not.
I'm Korean.

33
00:08:41.480 --> 00:08:43.770
- Are you going to Seattle too?
- You don't need to pay me back.

34
00:09:04.211 --> 00:09:05.211
Hey!

35
00:09:06.588 --> 00:09:09.298
Hey, Hello?

36
00:09:12.052 --> 00:09:13.602
See this watch?

37
00:09:22.312 --> 00:09:24.192
It means a lot to me.

38
00:09:24.773 --> 00:09:27.323
Keep it, until I pay you back.

39
00:09:29.861 --> 00:09:31.361
Don't lose it.

40
00:10:17.159 --> 00:10:18.199
Hello?

41
00:10:18.201 --> 00:10:19.541
<i>Where in the world are you?

42
00:10:19.870 --> 00:10:22.960
On the way to Seattle.
What'd you find out?

43
00:10:23.415 --> 00:10:25.875
<i>Did you ask Ok-ja for money?

44
00:10:26.376 --> 00:10:28.876
<i>Her husband is looking for you.

45
00:10:29.171 --> 00:10:30.881
<i>He's going to kill you.

46
00:10:31.173 --> 00:10:32.263
Why?

47
00:10:32.507 --> 00:10:35.257
<i>She took money and left home.

48
00:10:35.761 --> 00:10:39.061
<i>You know her husband.
He's dangerous.

49
00:10:40.057 --> 00:10:42.057
<i>He thinks you're with her.

50
00:10:44.394 --> 00:10:45.524
Really?

51
00:10:45.646 --> 00:10:50.316
<i>Well, don't meet any clients now
and be careful.

52
00:10:50.525 --> 00:10:51.435
Okay.

53
00:11:51.169 --> 00:11:52.209
Hey!

54
00:11:53.588 --> 00:11:55.168
I was looking for you.

55
00:11:55.632 --> 00:11:56.802
Why?

56
00:11:57.300 --> 00:11:58.720
I need the time.

57
00:12:20.323 --> 00:12:22.953
Still a long way to Seattle.

58
00:12:23.493 --> 00:12:24.663
Thank you.

59
00:12:33.879 --> 00:12:35.009
Hello?

60
00:13:39.236 --> 00:13:40.646
<i>Good, it's you.

61
00:13:40.654 --> 00:13:41.744
Any update?

62
00:13:41.738 --> 00:13:45.528
<i>It's not a joke.
He came again!

63
00:13:46.326 --> 00:13:47.576
<i>You need to hide somewhere.

64
00:13:47.577 --> 00:13:48.747
It's alright.

65
00:13:49.287 --> 00:13:50.537
<i>Man, you don't know shit.

66
00:13:51.331 --> 00:13:52.831
It's not the first time.

67
00:13:52.916 --> 00:13:55.706
<i>He's got people looking for you.

68
00:13:56.002 --> 00:13:58.592
This business is not
for scary-cats.

69
00:13:58.588 --> 00:14:03.678
<i>He's coming to get you!

70
00:14:05.554 --> 00:14:07.644
<i>Hello! Hello!

71
00:14:08.557 --> 00:14:12.937
Hello, hello, hello!

72
00:14:12.936 --> 00:14:14.056
<i>Hey, do you hear me?

73
00:14:14.771 --> 00:14:16.441
Tell him to catch me
if he can.

74
00:14:18.608 --> 00:14:20.528
I've been in America
2 years already.

75
00:14:20.652 --> 00:14:22.362
Don't you worry about me.

76
00:14:22.779 --> 00:14:27.699
My English got better,
so I'm thinking about expanding my client pool.

77
00:15:46.780 --> 00:15:48.450
Oh, no, no.
Keep it.

78
00:15:50.533 --> 00:15:52.493
I will get some cash and call you.

79
00:15:52.494 --> 00:15:53.754
What is your number?

80
00:15:54.871 --> 00:15:56.291
I don't have one.

81
00:15:57.415 --> 00:15:58.495
Wait.

82
00:16:04.214 --> 00:16:05.884
This is my number.

83
00:16:06.841 --> 00:16:10.011
I will pay you first
and then get my watch.

84
00:16:10.553 --> 00:16:12.723
So call me, okay?

85
00:16:20.563 --> 00:16:22.573
You will call me, right?

86
00:16:25.819 --> 00:16:26.989
Wait a minute.

87
00:16:27.237 --> 00:16:28.357
Call me.

88
00:16:31.449 --> 00:16:32.699
Oh, hi.

89
00:17:36.222 --> 00:17:37.722
You finally came!

90
00:17:40.810 --> 00:17:42.060
Anna's here!

91
00:17:42.062 --> 00:17:43.522
Look!

92
00:17:43.521 --> 00:17:44.271
Sit here.

93
00:17:44.272 --> 00:17:45.732
Sorry about not visiting you.

94
00:17:45.732 --> 00:17:47.322
We were worried that
you couldn't make it.

95
00:17:47.317 --> 00:17:48.607
It was a long trip,
wasn't it?

96
00:17:48.610 --> 00:17:49.740
You must be thirsty.

97
00:17:50.904 --> 00:17:54.624
Anna behaved well,
so bond could set her out.

98
00:17:54.991 --> 00:17:57.541
It's the first time
they gave bond to a murderer.

99
00:17:57.994 --> 00:17:59.164
Alex!

100
00:18:03.333 --> 00:18:04.753
Thank you for the bond money.

101
00:18:05.794 --> 00:18:08.134
Don't mention it.

102
00:18:08.129 --> 00:18:09.509
Have some tea.

103
00:18:09.506 --> 00:18:10.966
Yeah. Have some tea.

104
00:18:12.175 --> 00:18:13.755
You've lost some weight.

105
00:18:14.886 --> 00:18:16.296
Mommy!

106
00:18:16.304 --> 00:18:17.934
The kids are here.

107
00:18:18.848 --> 00:18:20.428
Come on.
Say hi to auntie.

108
00:18:20.433 --> 00:18:22.643
You know who she is, right?

109
00:18:22.644 --> 00:18:24.354
Say hi to auntie.
Hi.

110
00:18:25.313 --> 00:18:27.863
They can't speak Chinese.

111
00:18:28.358 --> 00:18:30.188
She's your auntie.

112
00:18:31.277 --> 00:18:32.737
<i>You know kids...

113
00:18:34.322 --> 00:18:36.742
Let them be.

114
00:18:37.867 --> 00:18:39.697
- Mommy come here!
- The kids have grown, haven't they?

115
00:18:39.702 --> 00:18:41.122
Oops, it's your first time
seeing the kids, right?

116
00:18:41.121 --> 00:18:43.411
I'm going to check up on the kids.

117
00:18:46.876 --> 00:18:48.496
Let me get the phone.

118
00:18:50.338 --> 00:18:52.168
Wait.
Oh, I have to watch the grill.

119
00:18:52.841 --> 00:18:54.381
I was cooking.

120
00:18:54.717 --> 00:18:56.257
I'll get you a snack.

121
00:19:45.393 --> 00:19:47.603
I wanted to talk to you.

122
00:19:47.854 --> 00:19:50.324
With mom gone,
the house is empty.

123
00:19:50.857 --> 00:19:54.107
And I need the money.
So I decided to sell the house.

124
00:19:54.110 --> 00:19:56.320
Of course,
we'll split the money.

125
00:19:56.321 --> 00:19:59.321
Equally, including you.

126
00:19:59.699 --> 00:20:06.749
So... I need you to sign here.
Take a look?

127
00:20:06.748 --> 00:20:08.248
What do you think?

128
00:20:17.926 --> 00:20:19.176
After you have tea.

129
00:20:19.969 --> 00:20:21.389
Some cookies too.

130
00:20:23.723 --> 00:20:26.183
What's happening
with the gravestone?

131
00:20:26.184 --> 00:20:28.314
- Right, the gravestone!
- Is it all set?

132
00:20:28.311 --> 00:20:31.441
- The gravestone...
- They said they couldn't fix it.

133
00:20:32.774 --> 00:20:34.404
Nothing we can do.

134
00:20:34.400 --> 00:20:35.690
What do you mean by that?

135
00:20:35.693 --> 00:20:37.113
We can't leave it like that?

136
00:20:37.111 --> 00:20:39.161
We have to fix it.

137
00:20:39.822 --> 00:20:41.742
Tell me how.

138
00:20:43.284 --> 00:20:45.254
Why don't you ask Anna?

139
00:20:45.245 --> 00:20:47.075
Why are you asking her that?

140
00:20:47.080 --> 00:20:48.920
She just got here.
What can she do?

141
00:20:50.583 --> 00:20:53.133
But she should know about it too.

142
00:20:54.379 --> 00:20:56.339
Okay, I'll tell her.

143
00:20:56.631 --> 00:20:59.181
Anna, please listen.

144
00:20:59.425 --> 00:21:02.795
John got mom's birthdate wrong
on her gravestone.

145
00:21:02.804 --> 00:21:04.354
What should we do?

146
00:21:04.389 --> 00:21:07.269
They made the mistake, not me.

147
00:21:07.350 --> 00:21:11.350
- That's besides the point.
- We still have to get it fixed.

148
00:21:11.354 --> 00:21:14.864
- You are the one who messed it up.
- What're you gonna do? The funeral is tomorrow.

149
00:21:14.857 --> 00:21:19.857
We can't go with the wrong date.

150
00:21:19.862 --> 00:21:22.242
But it's not my fault.

151
00:21:24.200 --> 00:21:26.200
You should've double checked.

152
00:21:26.202 --> 00:21:28.542
I've been busy with the house.

153
00:21:28.538 --> 00:21:31.288
What's more important?
Mom or the house?

154
00:21:31.332 --> 00:21:32.712
Hey calm down.

155
00:22:54.290 --> 00:22:55.710
How are you doing?

156
00:22:58.127 --> 00:23:00.047
It must've been hard getting here.

157
00:23:01.589 --> 00:23:03.929
I wasn't sure you could get out.

158
00:23:04.759 --> 00:23:06.639
You haven't changed a bit.

159
00:23:09.597 --> 00:23:11.017
Really?

160
00:23:12.809 --> 00:23:15.139
I'm sure I've changed a lot.

161
00:23:17.021 --> 00:23:19.771
Well, you still look like a kid.

162
00:23:21.442 --> 00:23:24.152
Do you still want that
kid to come back?

163
00:23:25.446 --> 00:23:26.656
What?

164
00:23:37.917 --> 00:23:40.087
Time really flies.

165
00:23:42.713 --> 00:23:45.173
A lot has happened.

166
00:23:47.635 --> 00:23:50.255
Not a lot has happened for me.

167
00:24:01.357 --> 00:24:06.357
By the time I tried to contact you.

168
00:24:07.238 --> 00:24:09.028
- It was already...
- It's over.

169
00:24:13.995 --> 00:24:15.365
Wang Jing.

170
00:24:18.332 --> 00:24:19.382
Are you coming?

171
00:24:19.375 --> 00:24:21.205
Ok?
I'll be right there.

172
00:24:22.545 --> 00:24:23.835
Ok.

173
00:25:15.765 --> 00:25:18.595
Honey.
I'm going to be late.

174
00:25:21.437 --> 00:25:23.437
I've left plenty on the table.

175
00:25:27.610 --> 00:25:31.160
You can look around Seattle.

176
00:25:32.240 --> 00:25:34.030
It's not a bad place for a visit.

177
00:25:35.993 --> 00:25:38.043
Though the weather can be erratic...

178
00:25:42.833 --> 00:25:44.463
I'll call you.

179
00:25:50.132 --> 00:25:51.382
What?

180
00:25:57.265 --> 00:25:58.635
Did you say something?

181
00:25:58.808 --> 00:26:02.978
Kilsoon, did you say something?

182
00:27:02.204 --> 00:27:04.124
No, that's not it.

183
00:29:24.180 --> 00:29:25.060
Hello.

184
00:29:25.055 --> 00:29:27.095
<i>CDCR number and location.

185
00:29:27.516 --> 00:29:31.346
Yes. Inmate 2537.
I'm in Seattle.

186
00:29:31.687 --> 00:29:34.687
<i>Yeah. Don't forget you need to
be back by tomorrow.

187
00:29:36.400 --> 00:29:39.360
Hello? Hello?

188
00:30:56.772 --> 00:30:57.402
Thank you.

189
00:30:57.439 --> 00:30:58.519
Thank you.

190
00:31:01.861 --> 00:31:03.491
Hi. Where to?

191
00:31:16.250 --> 00:31:19.340
- Hi.
- Hi. One for Baker's Field, please.

192
00:31:20.004 --> 00:31:21.054
$145.00

193
00:31:31.974 --> 00:31:33.314
Hello again.

194
00:31:39.231 --> 00:31:40.151
Hi.

195
00:31:40.274 --> 00:31:41.444
Where are you going?

196
00:32:22.316 --> 00:32:23.816
What time is it now?

197
00:32:29.698 --> 00:32:31.028
Oh, wait.

198
00:32:36.580 --> 00:32:37.830
Your money.

199
00:32:56.767 --> 00:32:58.017
Do you want me?

200
00:37:07.643 --> 00:37:09.103
Don't scratch.

201
00:37:10.312 --> 00:37:11.612
What?

202
00:37:12.564 --> 00:37:14.194
You'll make it worse.

203
00:37:25.035 --> 00:37:26.245
Sorry.

204
00:37:39.508 --> 00:37:40.718
It's okay.

205
00:37:41.969 --> 00:37:43.349
It's my fault.

206
00:37:45.847 --> 00:37:46.967
Hm?

207
00:37:47.015 --> 00:37:49.305
You're my first unhappy customer,

208
00:37:49.643 --> 00:37:53.023
so I'll give you a discount
for today.

209
00:37:55.023 --> 00:37:55.983
Ok?

210
00:37:58.527 --> 00:38:00.697
Nice to have company.
Right?

211
00:38:02.572 --> 00:38:04.032
Let's go.

212
00:38:40.485 --> 00:38:41.735
Stop raining.

213
00:39:06.178 --> 00:39:07.468
It's OK.

214
00:39:09.765 --> 00:39:11.425
Thanks for thinking of me.

215
00:39:17.356 --> 00:39:19.726
Sure, anytime's fine with me.

216
00:39:31.161 --> 00:39:32.621
What is it you do?

217
00:39:34.289 --> 00:39:36.119
Whatever she wants.

218
00:39:37.292 --> 00:39:40.382
I will be your escort
and show you a good time.

219
00:39:42.881 --> 00:39:46.091
We can go out,
go dance, go party.

220
00:39:47.219 --> 00:39:49.929
You want me to be good?
I'll be good.

221
00:39:51.473 --> 00:39:55.143
You want me to be bad?
I can be bad.

222
00:39:56.061 --> 00:39:58.151
Satisfaction guaranteed...

223
00:39:59.481 --> 00:40:01.901
or you don't have to pay.

224
00:40:27.676 --> 00:40:29.086
- Hi.
- Hi.

225
00:40:30.178 --> 00:40:31.678
- Two?
- Yes.

226
00:40:31.680 --> 00:40:33.890
- Come with me.
- I have a reservation.

227
00:40:34.808 --> 00:40:37.808
Oh, okay...
What is your name?

228
00:40:38.687 --> 00:40:41.817
You know,
my wife made the reservation.

229
00:40:41.815 --> 00:40:43.435
Today is my birthday.

230
00:40:43.733 --> 00:40:45.243
Oh!
Happy birthday!

231
00:40:45.235 --> 00:40:47.105
- Thank you.
- What is your name?

232
00:40:56.163 --> 00:40:58.543
I didn't make a reservation.

233
00:41:02.961 --> 00:41:04.251
That's ok.

234
00:41:04.254 --> 00:41:07.424
I can just take down your
reservation right now.

235
00:41:08.341 --> 00:41:09.801
What is your name?

236
00:41:18.560 --> 00:41:22.020
Anna. Anna Chen.

237
00:41:22.397 --> 00:41:24.267
Anna Chen...
is Beautiful name.

238
00:41:27.402 --> 00:41:30.782
What do you want to eat...
Anna?

239
00:41:31.698 --> 00:41:33.068
I'm Hoon.

240
00:41:43.752 --> 00:41:45.422
- Enjoy!
- Thank you.

241
00:42:25.710 --> 00:42:27.670
It tastes good, right?

242
00:42:40.517 --> 00:42:44.227
Today is my birthday,
so what will you do for me?

243
00:42:46.982 --> 00:42:52.822
To the right is a zoo.
Straight ahead is an amusement park.

244
00:42:53.238 --> 00:42:55.278
Or maybe shopping?

245
00:42:58.827 --> 00:43:00.697
Do you know Seattle well?

246
00:43:01.162 --> 00:43:02.412
Of course.

247
00:43:08.878 --> 00:43:12.088
Okay, I'll be your guide.

248
00:43:12.507 --> 00:43:15.177
So today, you follow me.

249
00:43:20.807 --> 00:43:23.137
There is just one thing
you all need to remember.

250
00:43:23.184 --> 00:43:25.524
You're never gonna see
any of these people again.

251
00:43:25.520 --> 00:43:27.440
So go head and
do anything you wanna do.

252
00:43:27.439 --> 00:43:29.479
What happens on the ducks?

253
00:43:29.482 --> 00:43:31.652
Stay on the duck!

254
00:43:32.444 --> 00:43:33.864
You guys ready to
get out of here?

255
00:43:43.204 --> 00:43:46.884
Seattle is the perfect place
to do this. Look around.

256
00:43:46.875 --> 00:43:48.625
It's a beautiful city.

257
00:43:48.627 --> 00:43:50.797
Ok, everybody get your quackers ready.

258
00:43:50.795 --> 00:43:54.545
If you don't have a quacker,
I wanna hear everybody clapping. Come on!

259
00:43:54.549 --> 00:43:58.719
Clap. Quack quack quack. Quack.
Come on. You like it? Don't you? Come on.

260
00:43:58.720 --> 00:44:00.180
Quackers come on.
We did it.

261
00:44:31.169 --> 00:44:33.509
Look around.
It's beautiful today.

262
00:44:33.505 --> 00:44:36.465
You know, Seattle is always foggy
and rainy this time a year.

263
00:44:36.466 --> 00:44:38.926
But, look, it's bright and
sunny out there all of a sudden.

264
00:44:38.927 --> 00:44:42.557
I don't know. Maybe you guys brought
the sunshine to us. Thanks a lot!

265
00:44:42.972 --> 00:44:45.432
You should enjoy the sun now,
because I tell you,

266
00:44:45.433 --> 00:44:48.313
it's gonna disappear soon.
Fog come back.

267
00:44:49.354 --> 00:44:52.274
Folks, the good time in our lives
don't last too long.

268
00:44:52.273 --> 00:44:57.283
So, take it manage the moment.
Open your heart and love it now!

269
00:45:09.207 --> 00:45:10.537
Not open.

270
00:45:10.792 --> 00:45:14.302
Strange...
It's supposed to be open.

271
00:45:21.678 --> 00:45:24.638
Hey.
Let's see up there.

272
00:48:02.755 --> 00:48:06.125
How?
How did you find me?

273
00:48:06.426 --> 00:48:07.756
Go away.

274
00:48:09.429 --> 00:48:13.139
I came all the way
from Greece to find you.

275
00:48:16.853 --> 00:48:19.693
You are so tiresome, woman.

276
00:48:21.858 --> 00:48:23.738
Don't look at me like that.

277
00:48:24.277 --> 00:48:28.567
No, this is how I always
look at you.

278
00:48:32.285 --> 00:48:33.825
Come back with me.

279
00:48:35.079 --> 00:48:38.329
No. I have a new life.

280
00:48:38.833 --> 00:48:42.503
Why? Why did you
come back to me again?

281
00:48:43.004 --> 00:48:50.934
I don't know.
All my love, my heart is here.

282
00:48:52.764 --> 00:48:58.484
Your heart? Don't make me laugh.
Stop fooling yourself.

283
00:48:58.937 --> 00:49:04.357
This is not love.
It is only memories and obsession.

284
00:49:10.907 --> 00:49:12.277
Please.

285
00:49:13.368 --> 00:49:15.448
Don't look at me like that.

286
00:49:15.578 --> 00:49:17.908
Why have you changed so?

287
00:49:23.503 --> 00:49:25.843
This is how I always look at you.

288
00:49:25.838 --> 00:49:28.338
No, that's not true.

289
00:49:29.092 --> 00:49:32.892
Your eyes,
they were always so warm.

290
00:49:35.390 --> 00:49:37.180
I can't remember.

291
00:49:37.809 --> 00:49:39.599
Try to remember.

292
00:49:40.144 --> 00:49:43.364
I can only remember
that I cannot forgive you.

293
00:49:45.858 --> 00:49:48.278
I am not asking
for your forgiveness.

294
00:49:48.361 --> 00:49:50.031
I want your love.

295
00:49:52.156 --> 00:49:53.866
You are so shameless.

296
00:49:53.866 --> 00:49:55.906
Yes, I am.

297
00:49:56.285 --> 00:49:58.405
But you made me this way.

298
00:49:58.413 --> 00:50:00.673
You told me to come back.

299
00:50:02.166 --> 00:50:03.996
I said nothing.

300
00:50:04.085 --> 00:50:05.545
But you did.

301
00:50:05.837 --> 00:50:10.217
Your eyes, your caress,
they all called me back to you.

302
00:50:10.466 --> 00:50:13.086
Some things do not have to be spoken.

303
00:50:27.316 --> 00:50:28.776
I have to go.

304
00:50:28.901 --> 00:50:31.611
Your happiness is in your hands now.

305
00:50:33.656 --> 00:50:36.276
You could never be so cruel.

306
00:51:02.143 --> 00:51:03.313
Wait!

307
00:54:16.545 --> 00:54:17.505
Wait!

308
00:55:39.253 --> 00:55:40.423
I...

309
00:55:43.174 --> 00:55:45.974
I have to go back to prison tomorrow,

310
00:55:48.262 --> 00:55:50.392
after my mother's funeral.

311
00:56:40.314 --> 00:56:41.484
Hao.

312
00:56:44.485 --> 00:56:49.525
Hao. That's the only word
I know in Chinese.

313
00:56:50.533 --> 00:56:53.413
It means 'bad', right?

314
00:56:57.415 --> 00:56:59.915
No, it means 'good'.

315
00:57:00.709 --> 00:57:02.039
Really?

316
00:57:04.630 --> 00:57:07.090
Then... how do you say 'bad'?

317
00:57:08.259 --> 00:57:09.429
Huai.

318
00:57:10.594 --> 00:57:13.184
Huai. Huai...

319
00:57:16.642 --> 00:57:20.692
Huai. Huai...

320
00:57:33.159 --> 00:57:36.369
I'm sorry,
we are doing a Ghost Tour.

321
00:57:36.620 --> 00:57:39.870
You never really know
what you'll run into around here.

322
00:57:40.207 --> 00:57:42.587
Come on, we're going to
go up to the mortuary.

323
00:58:13.073 --> 00:58:15.663
Market Ghost Tour.

324
00:58:18.245 --> 00:58:22.165
So... many ghosts here?

325
00:58:30.257 --> 00:58:31.507
Hao. (Good)

326
00:58:37.348 --> 00:58:38.768
Did you come here a lot?

327
00:58:42.645 --> 00:58:44.095
Hao. (Good)

328
00:58:48.609 --> 00:58:53.699
I used to come here a lot...
with someone.

329
00:58:56.992 --> 00:58:58.542
Hao. (Good)
Hao. (Good)

330
00:59:06.502 --> 00:59:08.592
He was a friend of my older brother.

331
00:59:09.505 --> 00:59:11.295
We grew up together.

332
00:59:16.637 --> 00:59:17.717
Hao. (Good)

333
00:59:17.721 --> 00:59:24.481
At that time,
without him I couldn't live.

334
00:59:28.315 --> 00:59:29.685
Huai. (Bad)

335
00:59:33.571 --> 00:59:38.831
But... Suddenly he left me.

336
00:59:41.954 --> 00:59:43.374
Hao. (Good)

337
00:59:43.831 --> 00:59:46.831
And I married someone else.

338
00:59:48.627 --> 00:59:50.417
At first,

339
00:59:50.754 --> 00:59:54.764
he was caring and loving.

340
00:59:56.677 --> 00:59:58.387
Huai. (Bad)

341
01:00:03.976 --> 01:00:05.976
But I found out later that...

342
01:00:08.522 --> 01:00:16.322
he was weak,
and was suspicious.

343
01:00:18.282 --> 01:00:20.622
I don't know how
I got through those days.

344
01:00:22.077 --> 01:00:23.327
Hao. (Good)

345
01:00:26.874 --> 01:00:28.424
One day

346
01:00:31.295 --> 01:00:33.835
my first love came back

347
01:00:37.092 --> 01:00:38.932
asking me to leave with him.

348
01:00:42.056 --> 01:00:43.426
Hao. (Good)

349
01:00:50.356 --> 01:00:55.686
Somehow my husband found out...

350
01:00:59.573 --> 01:01:03.243
he threatened to kill us.

351
01:01:08.916 --> 01:01:10.166
Huai. (Bad)

352
01:01:14.380 --> 01:01:15.800
That morning...

353
01:01:32.940 --> 01:01:39.240
He beat me so much
that I lost consciousness, and...

354
01:01:43.617 --> 01:01:44.947
Hao. (Good)

355
01:01:57.548 --> 01:02:01.968
Where did it all go wrong?

356
01:02:06.807 --> 01:02:08.097
Hao. (Good)
Hao. (Good)

357
01:02:28.829 --> 01:02:30.709
Why'd you ask me for the money?

358
01:02:32.666 --> 01:02:34.166
You were saying yes.

359
01:02:35.461 --> 01:02:36.881
No, I didn't.

360
01:02:38.297 --> 01:02:39.837
You were smiling.

361
01:02:42.843 --> 01:02:45.353
No, I wasn't smiling.

362
01:02:46.013 --> 01:02:47.563
You smiled.

363
01:02:49.892 --> 01:02:51.272
No.

364
01:02:51.643 --> 01:02:53.063
Yes, you did.

365
01:02:56.440 --> 01:02:58.280
- No.
- Yes.

366
01:02:59.526 --> 01:03:01.026
- No.
- Yes.

367
01:03:01.737 --> 01:03:03.027
- No.
- Yes.

368
01:03:07.201 --> 01:03:08.291
No.

369
01:03:10.537 --> 01:03:11.707
Fine.

370
01:03:29.181 --> 01:03:30.521
Hello.

371
01:03:40.359 --> 01:03:41.569
Where are you?

372
01:05:08.030 --> 01:05:09.530
Thanks for today.

373
01:05:12.993 --> 01:05:19.213
How much do you usually charge
to spend a day with someone.

374
01:05:31.345 --> 01:05:35.595
You owe me $30,
so how much minus that?

375
01:05:38.310 --> 01:05:39.690
Here's $10 more.

376
01:06:01.458 --> 01:06:04.628
Wait here.
Just half an hour.

377
01:06:06.922 --> 01:06:07.882
No.

378
01:06:07.881 --> 01:06:09.801
I'll be back very fast.

379
01:06:09.800 --> 01:06:11.720
No, I won't be here.

380
01:06:12.386 --> 01:06:13.716
I know.

381
01:06:16.473 --> 01:06:17.933
What do you know?

382
01:06:18.642 --> 01:06:20.392
That you won't be here.

383
01:07:03.103 --> 01:07:04.603
Oh, you came.

384
01:07:06.440 --> 01:07:07.940
You really came.

385
01:07:15.782 --> 01:07:18.202
Here it is.

386
01:07:20.328 --> 01:07:22.458
Your husband is looking for me.

387
01:07:23.331 --> 01:07:24.671
I know.

388
01:07:25.167 --> 01:07:27.127
Don't worry.

389
01:07:27.335 --> 01:07:31.545
He might look scary
but he's a good man.

390
01:07:35.761 --> 01:07:37.891
He said he's going to kill me.

391
01:07:43.351 --> 01:07:46.151
Let's stay together.

392
01:07:48.315 --> 01:07:50.475
You know I have a lot of money.

393
01:07:51.276 --> 01:07:55.066
Enough to help you
set up a restaurant.

394
01:07:57.908 --> 01:08:00.488
Why don't we run away together?

395
01:08:02.662 --> 01:08:03.872
I have to get going.

396
01:08:04.581 --> 01:08:06.001
Take the money.

397
01:08:13.715 --> 01:08:16.335
Now I've seen you, I'm happy.

398
01:08:18.095 --> 01:08:19.545
I know.

399
01:08:23.809 --> 01:08:25.639
Take the money.

400
01:08:26.311 --> 01:08:28.811
<i>Go.

401
01:09:04.057 --> 01:09:05.387
You should get some rest.

402
01:09:13.191 --> 01:09:16.071
It would be good
if we stay together, stupid.

403
01:09:16.903 --> 01:09:18.453
You're stupid.
You know that?

404
01:09:24.077 --> 01:09:27.497
<i>Ok. Bye.

405
01:12:21.296 --> 01:12:23.916
Mom, do you remember this?

406
01:12:34.684 --> 01:12:36.774
You taught me when I was young.

407
01:12:37.270 --> 01:12:38.980
But I'm not good like you.

408
01:12:45.862 --> 01:12:47.202
What do you think?

409
01:12:51.493 --> 01:12:52.993
Isn't it good?

410
01:12:55.538 --> 01:12:56.578
Mom.

411
01:12:59.626 --> 01:13:01.376
Ah, I forgot.

412
01:13:21.481 --> 01:13:25.571
Mom, Can you see?

413
01:13:28.238 --> 01:13:29.358
Here.

414
01:13:30.031 --> 01:13:31.321
See?

415
01:13:31.825 --> 01:13:34.865
Can you see without your glasses?

416
01:13:35.161 --> 01:13:36.201
Here.

417
01:13:37.997 --> 01:13:40.917
This is where I live now.

418
01:13:45.171 --> 01:13:46.971
The weather's really nice there.

419
01:14:16.786 --> 01:14:18.326
Don't worry about me.

420
01:16:29.502 --> 01:16:32.962
Sorry... who may you be?

421
01:16:40.388 --> 01:16:41.638
A friend.

422
01:16:42.348 --> 01:16:43.518
Thank you.

423
01:17:44.577 --> 01:17:45.697
<i>Well done...

424
01:17:49.957 --> 01:17:53.127
- That's all of it. Thanks.
- Everything's done, yes?

425
01:17:53.127 --> 01:17:54.297
Yes.

426
01:17:55.421 --> 01:17:56.841
Thanks, Anna.

427
01:17:58.925 --> 01:18:02.005
Don't worry about your share.

428
01:18:02.136 --> 01:18:03.096
John.

429
01:18:03.429 --> 01:18:04.509
Can you come here?

430
01:18:05.682 --> 01:18:07.022
I have to go.

431
01:18:13.231 --> 01:18:14.941
With mom gone...

432
01:18:14.941 --> 01:18:18.031
We should talk about the restaurant.

433
01:18:18.277 --> 01:18:22.117
In any case, we should get half,
shouldn't we?

434
01:18:22.281 --> 01:18:25.871
I understand.
Let's talk about it another time.

435
01:18:26.202 --> 01:18:28.002
What other time?

436
01:18:28.371 --> 01:18:31.121
It's always on your time.

437
01:18:31.124 --> 01:18:34.044
I have to follow your schedule?

438
01:19:09.245 --> 01:19:10.405
Thank you.

439
01:19:31.893 --> 01:19:33.813
Anna. Hi.

440
01:19:34.687 --> 01:19:36.267
Can I sit here?

441
01:19:38.191 --> 01:19:39.361
Thank you.

442
01:19:44.906 --> 01:19:49.866
Anna, I'm really sorry
about your loss.

443
01:19:53.873 --> 01:19:55.123
Thank you.

444
01:19:58.878 --> 01:20:00.548
- Hi.
- Hi.

445
01:20:03.382 --> 01:20:05.802
Wang Jing. Come here.

446
01:20:12.725 --> 01:20:17.475
Oh, so you met Anna.
Good. Good.

447
01:20:27.657 --> 01:20:31.197
So... I...
Me and Anna, we are...

448
01:20:31.869 --> 01:20:34.459
Yeah, I knew Anna
when she was just a little girl.

449
01:20:34.580 --> 01:20:38.380
And... she was such a smart girl,
she picked up English right away,

450
01:20:38.376 --> 01:20:39.456
didn't you, Anna?

451
01:20:42.255 --> 01:20:44.415
Actually, she used to work
at this restaurant.

452
01:20:44.632 --> 01:20:47.552
And when the customers would come in,
they would only ask for Anna.

453
01:20:47.593 --> 01:20:49.853
Within a few months
she was working the counter.

454
01:20:49.846 --> 01:20:51.846
You know,
so that everybody could talk to her.

455
01:20:54.517 --> 01:20:56.637
Anna, how is China these days?

456
01:20:58.020 --> 01:21:00.150
You've been there
for a while, right?

457
01:21:04.944 --> 01:21:10.494
Yes.
She's... she's been away.

458
01:21:15.454 --> 01:21:19.294
And, did you come
with her from China?

459
01:21:21.502 --> 01:21:22.712
Yes.

460
01:21:24.797 --> 01:21:26.257
So how is it there?

461
01:21:29.427 --> 01:21:32.967
You know, the economy,
it's not so good.

462
01:21:33.306 --> 01:21:37.886
So, a little hard.
But our restaurant, it is doing very nice.

463
01:21:39.145 --> 01:21:42.685
Everyone wants Anna.
They all ask for Anna.

464
01:21:42.982 --> 01:21:45.822
They are strange.
Very strange.

465
01:21:46.319 --> 01:21:48.149
People are strange.

466
01:21:48.154 --> 01:21:50.914
But sometimes,
strange people are good.

467
01:21:51.115 --> 01:21:53.865
I don't know why
but I like strange people.

468
01:22:00.666 --> 01:22:01.496
Sorry.

469
01:22:07.006 --> 01:22:07.876
Thank you.

470
01:22:20.061 --> 01:22:21.441
<i>We...

471
01:22:24.523 --> 01:22:27.743
Yeah, we're going to
get married soon.

472
01:22:28.694 --> 01:22:30.154
Really?

473
01:22:30.279 --> 01:22:31.359
Yes.

474
01:22:31.405 --> 01:22:34.025
In China, the Chinese way.

475
01:22:34.700 --> 01:22:40.500
Then I want to get married again
in America, the American way.

476
01:22:44.543 --> 01:22:46.093
Congratulations.

477
01:22:46.295 --> 01:22:47.505
Thank you.

478
01:22:49.924 --> 01:22:51.094
Wang Jing.

479
01:22:56.931 --> 01:22:59.271
Anna, could you please come?

480
01:23:03.437 --> 01:23:04.477
Sorry.

481
01:23:11.946 --> 01:23:14.566
I think I hear Liang Liang
I'm going to be right back.

482
01:23:14.573 --> 01:23:15.663
Ok.

483
01:23:25.084 --> 01:23:26.294
Who are you?

484
01:23:27.586 --> 01:23:30.756
Yes, I am with Anna from China.
We have a restaurant...

485
01:23:30.756 --> 01:23:33.506
No, who are you?

486
01:23:39.724 --> 01:23:41.484
Did you know her from before?

487
01:23:42.768 --> 01:23:44.268
Or did you just meet her?

488
01:23:52.445 --> 01:23:56.565
OK. It doesn't matter,
because I don't, I don't like you either way.

489
01:24:05.541 --> 01:24:07.081
Don't mess with Anna.

490
01:24:07.793 --> 01:24:09.633
She's had a very hard life.

491
01:24:10.796 --> 01:24:13.126
So she doesn't need you
to make it harder.

492
01:24:14.467 --> 01:24:15.927
Do you understand?

493
01:24:19.305 --> 01:24:21.015
Don't play games.

494
01:24:24.143 --> 01:24:26.103
Why not play games?

495
01:24:30.357 --> 01:24:31.977
Games are fun.

496
01:24:32.485 --> 01:24:34.145
They make her laugh.

497
01:24:34.361 --> 01:24:36.111
Do you make her laugh?

498
01:24:37.615 --> 01:24:39.905
Ok, You don't know
what you're talking about.

499
01:24:40.284 --> 01:24:41.664
You obviously don't know anything.

500
01:24:41.660 --> 01:24:43.330
I don't know.

501
01:24:45.039 --> 01:24:46.539
Why do I have to know?

502
01:24:46.624 --> 01:24:48.134
Ok, that's enough.

503
01:24:50.002 --> 01:24:51.422
We're not done.

504
01:24:59.428 --> 01:25:00.048
No, no, no, no, no.

505
01:25:00.054 --> 01:25:01.434
Nothing.

506
01:25:03.015 --> 01:25:03.765
What happened?

507
01:25:03.766 --> 01:25:04.766
Sorry.

508
01:25:05.101 --> 01:25:06.021
Ok?

509
01:25:06.894 --> 01:25:07.904
I'm fine.

510
01:25:08.395 --> 01:25:09.265
What is this?

511
01:25:09.730 --> 01:25:11.110
Calm down.

512
01:25:14.944 --> 01:25:18.414
Sorry, sorry, sorry.

513
01:25:23.202 --> 01:25:24.622
What are you doing here?

514
01:25:27.123 --> 01:25:28.713
What do you want with her?

515
01:25:29.291 --> 01:25:30.711
Show us some respect.

516
01:25:33.879 --> 01:25:37.379
Don't smile.
I don't like your smile.

517
01:25:37.967 --> 01:25:41.297
From now on,
you smile, you die.

518
01:25:44.723 --> 01:25:46.733
Break it up, you two!

519
01:25:52.898 --> 01:25:54.188
What are you doing?

520
01:26:09.915 --> 01:26:11.825
This man used my fork.

521
01:26:12.626 --> 01:26:17.086
And he's not even sorry.
Do you think that's right?

522
01:26:19.300 --> 01:26:23.350
He used my fork.
My fork!

523
01:26:41.822 --> 01:26:43.282
Wang Jing!

524
01:26:48.954 --> 01:26:50.794
Why did you use his fork?

525
01:26:58.839 --> 01:27:02.299
Tell me why,
why did you use his fork?

526
01:27:02.301 --> 01:27:04.601
Why did you use someone else's fork?

527
01:27:05.012 --> 01:27:08.312
You should apologize even if
you did it without knowing it.

528
01:27:08.307 --> 01:27:09.637
Do you know?

529
01:27:11.143 --> 01:27:13.853
Why? Tell me.
Why'd you use his fork?

530
01:27:13.938 --> 01:27:15.518
Why did you use his fork?

531
01:27:15.522 --> 01:27:16.942
Tell me.

532
01:27:16.941 --> 01:27:19.361
It's his.

533
01:27:19.360 --> 01:27:20.820
Not yours.

534
01:27:21.820 --> 01:27:24.320
Why? Why?

535
01:27:44.885 --> 01:27:47.845
I'm- I'm sorry.

536
01:27:57.731 --> 01:27:59.781
I'm sorry, I'm...

537
01:29:46.632 --> 01:29:47.762
No.

538
01:29:48.717 --> 01:29:50.177
To remember.

539
01:29:51.970 --> 01:29:53.720
I have many watches.

540
01:30:00.104 --> 01:30:01.314
Goodbye.

541
01:31:56.720 --> 01:31:57.850
Hello?

542
01:32:01.850 --> 01:32:05.270
Oh, I'm sorry.
My mistake.

543
01:32:07.105 --> 01:32:09.105
I thought you were someone else.

544
01:32:23.455 --> 01:32:25.075
I like your smile.

545
01:32:30.087 --> 01:32:32.257
Nice to meet you.
I'm Hoon.

546
01:32:36.885 --> 01:32:38.545
Nice to meet you.
I'm Anna.

547
01:32:41.473 --> 01:32:44.273
I'm here from Korea
to open a restaurant.

548
01:32:44.393 --> 01:32:45.733
What about you?

549
01:32:46.603 --> 01:32:53.193
I'm on vacation.
I'm about to return to China.

550
01:32:54.945 --> 01:32:57.815
